assistant: Subject: Read unit_amount when vendor omits price

Vendor API version 2026-10-01 sends a product's price as `unit_amount` instead of `price`. get_product only read `p.price`, and its `?? null` fallback hid the missing field, so p-1001 came back with `price: null`. The fix adds `unit_amount` to the `VendorProduct` type in `src/tools/get_product.ts` and maps `price: p.price ?? p.unit_amount ?? null`. The amount is passed through in US dollars as before: v1 sent `price: 1199` for this product and v2 sends `unit_amount: 1199`, so they match. The v1 response still sets `price`, so its fixture output is unchanged. typecheck, lint and test all pass. search_products also reads `p.price` directly. I didn't change it because nothing recorded shows what its v2 response looks like, but if v2 renamed the field there too, prices would go missing from search results as well.

Subject: Read unit_amount when vendor omits price

